# Redis Stack server configuration for the integrated stack.
#
# Copy this file to `redis.integrated.conf.local` in the repository root and replace the value
# there. compose.integrated.yml mounts that file read-only at `/redis-stack.conf`, which is the
# only path this image's own `/entrypoint.sh` reads (sealed evidence:
# tutorial/v2-j1-knowledge/frozen/image-entry-evidence/entrypoint.sh.txt:8-10). Without it the
# entrypoint starts redis-server with no configuration at all, so `/redis-stack.conf` is where
# access control has to be declared - not in command arguments, and not in REDIS_ARGS.
#
# What the checked-in preflight requires of the copy, and refuses otherwise:
#   * the file exists, is readable and is not empty;
#   * exactly one `requirepass` line, starting at the beginning of the line;
#   * a value that is one unquoted token of allowed characters, at least 32 bytes long;
#   * a value that is not this file's placeholder.
# So this example is safe to commit precisely because starting the stack with it still fails.
#
# Keep the value to yourself: the copy ends in `.local`, which is the suffix both .gitignore and
# .dockerignore match, and the healthcheck reads it out of this file instead of taking it from
# the environment or the command line.

requirepass REPLACE_WITH_A_RANDOM_SECRET_OF_AT_LEAST_32_BYTES
